A||||8||MinnGreenGT||Internal or External Balance?||||1||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||11:11 AM||||I'm running a 3.1L in my GT- the original motor was out of a Lumina Minivan (FWD), don't know what year.  I'm interested in getting the Fiero Store's undersized pulley kit. BUT I'm not sure if the 3.1 is internally balanced or externally- and whether or not this piece will work.  Anyone know? I emailed the Fiero Store, but have never recieved any response (gee...thanks).  Anyone?<P>Item description: <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=52304&variation=&aitem=3&mitem=3" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=52304&variat ion=&aitem=3&mitem=3</A><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spiff||09-13-2001||11:20 AM||||Here is the summit part # and price ASP-845202 PULLEY SET 69.39. I think you will have to call to do a special order.<BR>Also here is a link to ASP and there e-mail address <A HREF="http://www.aspracing.com/intro.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aspracing.com/intro.htm</A>       asp@aspracing.com  <P>I got this in my archived e-mail.<BR>Hope this help you in some way||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||09-13-2001||11:21 AM||||all 88 and later motor are internal balanced<BR>look for build date code on block.<BR>i think all 3.4 and 3.1 plus 88 2.8 are internal <BR>have heard that knocking off balance weight on pre88 flywheel/flexplate will make it useable for internal motor but rebalancing maybe good idea after removal of weight.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spiff||09-13-2001||11:24 AM|||| Fiero Year Engine Pulley Description Full Charge Hard<BR>Blk Alum <BR>85-88 2.8 25% Crank 900 RPM ASP845200<BR>$59.95 <BR>85-88 2.8 25% Crank<BR>23% Alternator 1100 RPM ASP845202<BR>$79.95 <P><BR>Sorry. They changed thier prices.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||12:00 PM||||Spiff-<P>Thanks for the reference... I emailed ASP asking if I should use the 25% Crank pulley for the 2.8,3.1,3.4 Camaro application (Since my motor is not an '84-'88 2.8).  I'll post the response when I recieve it!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||09-13-2001||12:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>I'm running a 3.1L in my GT- the original motor was out of a Lumina Minivan (FWD), don't know what year.  I'm interested in getting the Fiero Store's undersized pulley kit. BUT I'm not sure if the 3.1 is internally balanced or externally- and whether or not this piece will work.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You are asking Apples and IBMs ... the pulleys bolt on to the harmonic balancer and both are neutrally balanced  on any of the 60* so they can be used on ANY of the 60* engines.  The only thing that is externally balanced is the flywheel/flexplate and in anything other than the early 2.8, it is neutrally balanced.<P>The bolt pattern is the same for the pulleys so that isn't a problem.<P>The differences in the harmonic balancers is where GM put the marks to locate TDC so it can be timed.<P>BTW, where did you put the vacuum line from the modulator of the 440T4 transaxle?<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>Paul Herder<BR>88 Formula - Artero kit car doner and 350 TPI<BR>86 SE - 3.2 w/440T4 Transaxle<BR>95 GMC - 350 TBI - Factory "Custom"<BR>92 Mazda Protege - Stock<BR>55 Jones - First Edition WIFE- all mods, equipment,updates :D<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pherder:<BR><B> BTW, where did you put the vacuum line from the modulator of the 440T4 transaxle?<P>Paul<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Paul-<P>Strangely enough, GM_Parts_Guy asked me that same question on Sunday at Fierorama!?  I honestly don't know, my Dad was the mechanic on the project and I did very little myself.  I will call him and see what I can find out...  or you can email him at GTcharli@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000007||pherder||09-13-2001||05:33 PM||||Rob,<P>Got an e-mail from the guru himself, Ed Parks that he remembers "T"ing into the vacuum fitting by the distributor.<P>I tried that AND replaced the ECM (it was giving me some weird scan indications), adjusted the mechanical throttle stop and now things are starting to work as I think they should.<P>It doesn't BANG into reverse and 2-1 downshift is smooth now ... again not another bang as it downshifts.  <P>Now I just got to fine tune the TV and vacuum modulator adjustments and find out why I am not locking the TCC (computer says it is locked but when I push on the brakes at a steady speed (all other requirements for lock up are met) all I do is start to slow down ... the rpms do not rise as they should when the TCC is disengaged.<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>Paul Herder<BR>88 Formula - Artero kit car doner and 350 TPI<BR>86 SE - 3.2 w/440T4 Transaxle<BR>95 GMC - 350 TBI - Factory "Custom"<BR>92 Mazda Protege - Stock<BR>55 Jones - First Edition WIFE- all mods, equipment,updates :D<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135||||reg||6
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||09:54 PM||||Paul-<P>Not sure if you saw this thread I posted earlier today after talking with my Dad (mechanic). <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013636.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013636.html</A><P>How did you rewire the TCC plug?  I haven't even had a chance to try!<P>Ed if you're reading this... email me too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
